  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Port convex support faces and full 3D polygonal clipping, including edge-edge contacts and flipped candidate frames.",
  "regressions": [
    "Seven live support-face fixtures cover all seven convex tags over 24 directions, signed-zero/ties, cylinder thresholds, capsule radius-zero cases and guarded indexed hull ranges with degenerate faces.",
    "Six live clipping fixtures cover all 25 feature-cardinality pairs, degenerate edges, parallel/crossing edges, rotations, prediction thresholds and both output frames.",
    "Independent shape/feature hull checks and exact copied support vertices reject invalid outputs even if they match the supplied reference arrays."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Feature and manifold diagnostic offsets are exported from native repr(C) records and native contact fields.",
    "GJK, EPA and convex support initial bounds now use Rust-exported MAX_FLT (1e18), replacing an IEEE-f32 maximum literal. This preserves behavior within the existing coordinate/direction bounds while keeping the reference constant explicit.",
    "Generic flipped candidates are transformed before native manifold reduction, preserving its operation order.",
    "The existing cuboid contact caller explicitly selects the unflipped path. General PFM composition remains in progress."
  ],
  "related_changes": [
    "0043-convex-epa",
    "0042-epa-origin-roundoff"
  ]
}
